---
import styles from "./AiNotice.module.css"

/**
 * Disclosure shown at the top of entries that were built with AI help.
 * Clicking it expands a short note on how I use AI in my projects.
 */
---

<details class={styles.notice}>
  <summary class={styles.summary}>
    <span class={styles.icon} aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="currentColor">
        <path
          d="M11 2.5c.4 3.9 2.6 6.1 6.5 6.5-3.9.4-6.1 2.6-6.5 6.5-.4-3.9-2.6-6.1-6.5-6.5 3.9-.4 6.1-2.6 6.5-6.5Z"
        ></path>
        <path
          d="M18.5 13.5c.2 1.9 1.1 2.8 3 3-1.9.2-2.8 1.1-3 3-.2-1.9-1.1-2.8-3-3 1.9-.2 2.8-1.1 3-3Z"
        ></path>
      </svg>
    </span>
    <span class={styles.heading}>
      <span class={styles.label}>AI-assisted</span>
      <span class={styles.text}>
        This project was built with the help of Claude, an AI assistant.
      </span>
    </span>
    <span class={styles.toggle}>
      <span class={styles.toggleText}>How I use AI</span>
      <svg
        class={styles.chevron}
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        width="16"
        height="16"
        fill="none"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="2"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        <path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path>
      </svg>
    </span>
  </summary>

  <div class={styles.content}>
    <p>
      In my spare time I build things that make everyday life a bit better,
      from GNOME extensions and home servers to small changes on my car or
      house. AI helps with a lot of it: spotting pitfalls, improving ideas and
      filling in the gaps when I'm working with something new.
    </p>
    <p>
      I don't shy away from useful tools, and AI is one of them. If something
      can be done better, understood quicker or built with fewer mistakes, it
      would be foolish to reject it. I still make the decisions, keep learning
      and always verify the result.
    </p>
  </div>
</details>
